\begin_layout Abstract
SANCHO computes the current–voltage characteristics of a tight-binding chain with an on-site Hubbard interaction,
 coupled to two leads.
 It uses self-consistent non-equilibrium Green's functions (NEGF),
 with the interaction treated to zeroth,
 first (Hartree–Fock),
 second or third order in
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

.
 Spin is not resolved:
 the chain is paramagnetic and the current carries a factor of two for spin.
 Unlike QUICHOTTE,
 which evaluates the second order by FFT,
 SANCHO evaluates every order through factorised particle–hole and particle–particle 
\emph on
bubbles
\emph default
,
 which is what makes the third order affordable.
 SANCHO lives in the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
SANCHO/
\end_layout

\end_inset

 folder of the QUICHOTTE repository but is a complete,
 independent code with its own build,
 tests and examples.
 
\end_layout

