\begin_layout Section
Self-consistency
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The SCF machinery is the same as in QUICHOTTE and lives in the shared files 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
common/broyden_mixing.f90
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
common/scf_checks.f90
\end_layout

\end_inset

:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Formula $\Gr$
\end_inset

 and the independent half of 
\begin_inset Formula $\Gl$
\end_inset

 (anti-Hermitian) on the whole grid are packed into a real vector 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

;
 the residual is 
\begin_inset Formula $F(x)=x_{\text{out}}(x)-x$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Formula $F=0$
\end_inset

 is solved by Johnson's modified Broyden mixing (Phys.
\begin_inset space \space{}
\end_inset

Rev.
\begin_inset space \space{}
\end_inset

B 
\series bold
38
\series default
,
 12807 (1988)),
 with weight 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
alpha_mix
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 a ring buffer of 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
nhist
\end_layout

\end_inset

 steps (0 = linear mixing) and regulariser 
\begin_inset Formula $w_{0}=0.01$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{n+1}=x_{n}+\alpha F_{n}-\sum_{k}\gamma_{k}u_{k}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\gamma=(w_{0}^{2}\mathbb{1}+\Delta F^{T}\Delta F)^{-1}\Delta F^{T}F_{n}$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Converged when 
\begin_inset Formula $\max|F|<\code{tolf}$
\end_inset

,
 tested before mixing;
 at most 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
maxscf
\end_layout

\end_inset

 steps.
 The history is in 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
scf_V_<V>.dat
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Sanity checks after every step,
 for every site:
 occupation 
\begin_inset Formula $n_{i}=-i\hbar\,p\sum_{k}\Gl_{ii}$
\end_inset

 and spectral weight 
\begin_inset Formula $W_{i}=-\hbar\,(\delta/\pi)\sum_{k}\operatorname{Im}\Gr_{ii}$
\end_inset

.
 NaN or 
\begin_inset Formula $n_{i}\notin[-1,2]$
\end_inset

 abandons the voltage;
 
\begin_inset Formula $n_{i}\notin[-0.05,1.05]$
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Formula $W_{i}<0.5$
\end_inset

 rejects a converged solution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The first voltage starts from the non-interacting 
\begin_inset Formula $G_{0}$
\end_inset

.
 With 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
continuation = T
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (the default) every later voltage starts from the previous converged one;
 a failed voltage is flagged (column 3 
\begin_inset Formula $=0$
\end_inset

),
 and the next one starts from 
\begin_inset Formula $G_{0}$
\end_inset

.
 Exit code 3 if any voltage failed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Continuation pays off for small 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
delv
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 For coarse voltage steps it can start too far from the new solution (the Broyden iteration may then oscillate);
 use 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
continuation = F
\end_layout

\end_inset

 in that case.
\end_layout

